      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-236889",
      ":question/problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X \\ge x) = 0.95$, where $X\u223cF(\u03bd_{1}, \u03bd_{2})$.\n\n| $\u03bd_{2}\u2216\u03bd_{1}$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $6$ | $0.233$ | $0.259$ | $0.279$ | $0.296$ | $0.311$ |\n| $7$ | $0.238$ | $0.264$ | $0.286$ | $0.304$ | $0.319$ |\n| $8$ | $0.241$ | $0.268$ | $0.291$ | $0.310$ | $0.326$ |\n| $9$ | $0.244$ | $0.272$ | $0.295$ | $0.315$ | $0.331$ |\n| $10$ | $0.246$ | $0.275$ | $0.299$ | $0.319$ | $0.336$ |\n\nGiven that $X\u223cF(7, 10)$, find the value $c$ such that $P(X \\ge c) = 0.05$. Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
